[claims]

## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Kilo is a lightweight text editor that initializes terminal raw mode, detects window dimensions, and opens a single target file passed via the command line.
  > README.md:4 #292daf6ba680
  > README.md:8 #4c6b68363986
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
#c2[overview,i5] The main event loop drives editor execution by repeatedly refreshing the display and processing keypresses read directly from standard input without relying on curses.
  > README.md:16-17 #efb6b4eb18e1
  > kilo.c::editorReadKey #1235ba3b05b0
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
#c3[overview,i5] Screen rendering relies on standard VT100 escape sequences batched into a buffer and written in a single call, reserving two lines for status and message bars.
  > README.md:16-17 #efb6b4eb18e1
  > kilo.c:996 #b17ac450cac1
  > kilo.c:977 #2ed6dc6f2d15
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
#c4[overview,i5] Window resize events dynamically refresh screen dimensions via ioctl fallbacks or SIGWINCH handling, clamping the cursor position within visible boundaries.
  > kilo.c::getWindowSize #ad4a693ad779
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
  > kilo.c::handleSigWinCh #9b64b04397af
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
#c5[overview,i5] Text modifications insert, pad, or delete rows in the core editor state while setting dirty flags to track unsaved changes.
  > kilo.c::editorInsertRow #ee0d5fc82d49
  > kilo.c::editorDelRow #85721087ecca
  > kilo.c::editorRowInsertChar #d6c3990144bd
#c6[overview,i5] Syntax highlighting patterns are selected based on filename extensions and propagate dynamically across subsequent rows when multi-line comment states change.
  > kilo.c:513-515 #f2219efbdc81
  > kilo.c::editorSelectSyntaxHighlight #9dc867cf550c
#c7[overview,i5] Searching via CTRL-F allows string navigation while preserving the original cursor position and syntax highlighting state upon pressing ESC.
  > README.md:12-14 #af9f24d591ea
  > kilo.c:1044-1047 #d9b7d964c0d6
#c8[overview,i5] Safety mechanisms guard against accidental data loss by ignoring CTRL-C, requiring multiple consecutive CTRL-Q presses to exit dirty buffers, and resetting dirty flags on save.
  > README.md:12-14 #af9f24d591ea
  > kilo.c::editorSave #a9e9709084c7
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02

## (root)
#c9[i5] Kilo is a small text editor implemented in fewer than 1,000 lines of code as measured by cloc.
  > README.md:4 #292daf6ba680
#c10[i3] Kilo is invoked via the command line using the syntax kilo <filename>.
  > README.md:8 #4c6b68363986
#c11[i4] Keybindings in Kilo include CTRL-S to save, CTRL-Q to quit, and CTRL-F to search for a string.
  > README.md:12-14 #af9f24d591ea
#c12[i5] Kilo does not depend on external libraries like curses and relies on standard VT100 escape sequences.
  > README.md:16-17 #efb6b4eb18e1
#c13[i3] Kilo is in alpha stage and incorporates code adapted from the load81 and linenoise projects.
  > README.md:17-19 #0c5274601a06
#c14[i4] Kilo was created by Salvatore Sanfilippo (antirez) and distributed under the BSD 2-clause license.
  > README.md:25-26 #1738738f099b
#c15[i4] enableRawMode switches the terminal to raw mode, configures a 100 ms read timeout, and registers editorAtExit using atexit.
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
#c16[i3] editorReadKey aborts the process with exit(1) if read() returns -1 on the terminal file descriptor.
  > kilo.c::editorReadKey #1235ba3b05b0
#c17[i3] getWindowSize falls back to moving the cursor to bottom-right margins and querying its position if the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl fails.
  > kilo.c::getWindowSize #ad4a693ad779
#c18[i4] If a line's open multi-line comment state changes during syntax highlighting, editorUpdateSyntax recursively triggers syntax updates on subsequent rows.
  > kilo.c:513-515 #f2219efbdc81
#c19[i4] editorSelectSyntaxHighlight checks filename matches, enforcing suffix-only matching if a pattern begins with a dot.
  > kilo.c::editorSelectSyntaxHighlight #9dc867cf550c
#c20[i3] editorUpdateRow terminates the program with exit(1) if the calculated render allocation size exceeds UINT32_MAX.
  > kilo.c::editorUpdateRow #298eb05dee6b
#c21[i4] editorInsertRow inserts an erow at index 'at', shifting subsequent rows right, reallocating E.row, and setting its idx and initial fields.
  > kilo.c::editorInsertRow #ee0d5fc82d49
#c22[i3] editorDelRow frees the row's heap buffers, shifts subsequent rows left using memmove, decrements E.numrows, and increments E.dirty.
  > kilo.c::editorDelRow #85721087ecca
#c23[i3] editorRowInsertChar pads with spaces if the insert position exceeds row size, then updates the row and increments E.dirty.
  > kilo.c::editorRowInsertChar #d6c3990144bd
#c24[i4] editorOpen exits the program if opening filename fails with an error other than ENOENT.
  > kilo.c::editorOpen #a74a759a7b82
#c25[i4] editorSave flushes the rows string to disk using ftruncate and a single write, resetting E.dirty to 0 on success.
  > kilo.c::editorSave #a9e9709084c7
#c26[i4] editorRefreshScreen batches escape sequences into an abuf buffer and writes them to STDOUT_FILENO in a single write call.
  > kilo.c:996 #b17ac450cac1
#c27[i3] The second status bar row only renders E.statusmsg if it is non-empty and set within the last 5 seconds.
  > kilo.c:977 #2ed6dc6f2d15
#c28[i3] Pressing ESC during editorFind restores the saved cursor position (cx, cy, coloff, rowoff) and previous syntax highlighting.
  > kilo.c:1044-1047 #d9b7d964c0d6
#c29[i4] When unsaved changes exist in E.dirty, editorProcessKeypress requires pressing Ctrl-Q three consecutive times (KILO_QUIT_TIMES) to exit.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
#c30[i3] Any keypress other than a repeated Ctrl-Q resets quit_times back to KILO_QUIT_TIMES.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
#c31[i2] editorProcessKeypress intentionally ignores CTRL_C to prevent accidental loss of file changes.
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
#c32[i4] updateWindowSize subtracts 2 from E.screenrows to reserve room for the status bar.
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
#c33[i3] handleSigWinCh updates the window size, clamps E.cy and E.cx to screen boundaries, and redraws the screen.
  > kilo.c::handleSigWinCh #9b64b04397af
#c34[i4] initEditor zeroes editor state offsets and counters, calls updateWindowSize, and installs handleSigWinCh for SIGWINCH.
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
#c35[i3] main requires exactly one argument representing the filename, exiting with status 1 if argc != 2.
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
#c36[i4] The main event loop continuously calls editorRefreshScreen and editorProcessKeypress on STDIN_FILENO.
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31

[probes]
?p1 How many lines of code does Kilo have according to cloc?
  = Less than 1K lines
  > README.md:4 #292daf6ba680
?p2 What error code is assigned to errno when enableRawMode fails because standard input is not a tty?
  = ENOTTY
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
?p3 What permissions does editorSave pass to open() when creating or opening the file?
  = 0644
  > kilo.c::editorSave #a9e9709084c7
?p4 What is the initial value of KILO_QUIT_TIMES?
  = 3
  > kilo.c:1187 #bddc20b86e60
?p5 What key combination is used to find a string in Kilo?
  = CTRL-F
  > README.md:14 #a0280e8f56cc
?p6 What integer code does editorSyntaxToColor return for HL_NUMBER?
  = 31
  > kilo.c::editorSyntaxToColor #819747c749b1
?p7 How long in seconds does E.statusmsg remain visible on the screen?
  = Less than 5 seconds
  > kilo.c:977 #2ed6dc6f2d15
?p8 What does editorProcessKeypress do when receiving CTRL_C?
  = It ignores it (breaks with no action).
  > kilo.c::editorProcessKeypress #1164e28a1a02
?p9 Which terminal escape sequences does Kilo use?
  = VT100 (and similar terminals) escape sequences
  > README.md:17 #ce6f8d037e58
?p10 Which terminal escape code is sent by getWindowSize to move to the right and bottom margins?
  = \x1b[999C\x1b[999B
  > kilo.c::getWindowSize #ad4a693ad779
?p11 Which error code allows editorOpen to return 1 instead of calling exit(1)?
  = ENOENT
  > kilo.c::editorOpen #a74a759a7b82
?p12 How many rows does updateWindowSize subtract from E.screenrows for the status bar?
  = 2
  > kilo.c::updateWindowSize #6516dd852835
?p13 From which two projects was code taken to write Kilo?
  = load81 and linenoise
  > README.md:19 #218d3c6b465a
?p14 What terminal key code is returned by editorReadKey when processing the escape sequence ESC [ 3 ~?
  = DEL_KEY
  > kilo.c::editorReadKey #1235ba3b05b0
?p15 What maximum query length is defined for editorFind?
  = 256
  > kilo.c:1012 #f8ea1756a445
?p16 Which signal handler is registered in initEditor?
  = handleSigWinCh for SIGWINCH.
  > kilo.c::initEditor #880014f10916
?p17 Who is the author of Kilo?
  = Salvatore Sanfilippo aka antirez
  > README.md:25 #c3d14ae25009
?p18 To what multiple of columns are TAB characters expanded in editorUpdateRow?
  = 8
  > kilo.c::editorUpdateRow #298eb05dee6b
?p19 What three heap buffers does editorFreeRow deallocate?
  = render, chars, and hl
  > kilo.c::editorFreeRow #001586e3311a
?p20 What does editorFileWasModified return?
  = E.dirty
  > kilo.c::editorFileWasModified #f0e785df3c1d
?p21 Under what license is Kilo released?
  = BSD 2 clause license
  > README.md:26 #fe6c5ed874ed
?p22 Under what condition does editorRowHasOpenComment return 1?
  = When the row ends with HL_MLCOMMENT and its last two characters are not '*/'.
  > kilo.c::editorRowHasOpenComment #9ba007284bf7
?p23 When deleting a char at column 0 in editorDelChar, how is the current row merged?
  = Appended to the end of the previous row via editorRowAppendString, then removed via editorDelRow
  > kilo.c::editorDelChar #9311d4da2443
?p24 How many arguments does kilo expect on the command line?
  = Exactly 2 (the program name and one filename).
  > kilo.c::main #846ece275c31
?p25 What timeout value is set in raw.c_cc[VTIME] within enableRawMode?
  = 1 (representing 100 ms)
  > kilo.c::enableRawMode #cd72cf1e3c04
?p26 What escape sequence is appended by abAppend to hide the cursor during screen refresh?
  = \x1b[?25l
  > kilo.c:888 #96dfaf825f22
?p27 What function is invoked by disableRawMode to restore the original terminal attributes?
  = tcsetattr
  > kilo.c::disableRawMode #5a42b21c44df
?p28 How does editorRefreshScreen calculate tab indentation when computing cx?
  = cx += 7-((cx)%8)
  > kilo.c:989 #57ffbb27c584
